{"name":"Rocky Mountain","hex":"#a9867d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Rocky Mountain","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["singular of Rocky Mountains"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Rocky_Mountain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rocky Mountains","blocks":[{"text":"The Rocky Mountains, also known as the Rockies, are a major mountain range and the largest mountain system in North America. The Rocky Mountains stretch 3,000 mi (4,800 km) in a straight-line distance from the northernmost part of Western Canada, to New Mexico in the Southwestern United States. Depending on differing definitions between Canada and the U.S., its northern terminus is located either in northern British Columbia's Terminal Range south of the Liard River and east of the Trench, or in the northeastern foothills of the Brooks Range/British Mountains that face the Beaufort Sea coasts between the Canning River and the Firth River across the Alaska–Yukon border. Its southernmost point is near the Albuquerque metropolitan area, adjacent to the Rio Grande rift, and north of the Sandia–Manzano Mountain Range, also near Santa Fe, New Mexico. Being the easternmost portion of the North American Cordillera, the Rockies are distinct from the tectonically younger Cascade Range and Sierra Nevada, which both lie farther to its west."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Maroon_Bells_%2811553%29a.jpg/330px-Maroon_Bells_%2811553%29a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocky_Mountains","wikidata":"Q5463"},{"title":"Rocky","blocks":[{"text":"Rocky is a 1976 American sports drama film directed by John G. Avildsen and written by and starring Sylvester Stallone. It is the first installment in the Rocky film series and also stars Talia Shire, Burt Young, Carl Weathers, and Burgess Meredith. In the film, Rocky Balboa (Stallone), a poor small-time club fighter and loanshark debt collector from Philadelphia, gets an unlikely once in a lifetime shot at the world heavyweight championship held by Apollo Creed (Weathers)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/Rocky_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocky","wikidata":"Q188652"},{"title":"Mountain","blocks":[{"text":"A mountain is an elevated portion of the surface of a planet, generally with steep sides that show significant exposed bedrock. Although there are no universally accepted definitions, a mountain is usually considered higher than a hill. By definition, mountains are often thought of as being a landform which is higher than 2,000 feet (610 m). It may either have a limited summit area or be a smaller plateau with high elevation and steep sides. A few mountains are isolated summits, but most occur in mountain ranges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg/330px-Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain","wikidata":"Q8502"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2d/Southern_Terminus_of_the_Rocky_Mountains_from_the_Sandia_Mountains_of_North_Central_NM.jpg/500px-Southern_Terminus_of_the_Rocky_Mountains_from_the_Sandia_Mountains_of_North_Central_NM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2d/Southern_Terminus_of_the_Rocky_Mountains_from_the_Sandia_Mountains_of_North_Central_NM.jpg/1280px-Southern_Terminus_of_the_Rocky_Mountains_from_the_Sandia_Mountains_of_North_Central_NM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2d/Southern_Terminus_of_the_Rocky_Mountains_from_the_Sandia_Mountains_of_North_Central_NM.jpg/500px-Southern_Terminus_of_the_Rocky_Mountains_from_the_Sandia_Mountains_of_North_Central_NM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Santa Fe Mountains at the southern end of the Rockies as seen from the Sandia Crest in New Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASouthern_Terminus_of_the_Rocky_Mountains_from_the_Sandia_Mountains_of_North_Central_NM.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Willow_Flats_area_and_Teton_Range_in_Grand_Teton_National_Park.jpg/500px-Willow_Flats_area_and_Teton_Range_in_Grand_Teton_National_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Willow_Flats_area_and_Teton_Range_in_Grand_Teton_National_Park.jpg/1280px-Willow_Flats_area_and_Teton_Range_in_Grand_Teton_National_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Willow_Flats_area_and_Teton_Range_in_Grand_Teton_National_Park.jpg/500px-Willow_Flats_area_and_Teton_Range_in_Grand_Teton_National_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The summits of the Teton Range in Wyoming","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWillow_Flats_area_and_Teton_Range_in_Grand_Teton_National_Park.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Mount_Robson_Twilight.jpg/500px-Mount_Robson_Twilight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Mount_Robson_Twilight.jpg/500px-Mount_Robson_Twilight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mount Robson in British Columbia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMount_Robson_Twilight.jpg"},{"srcset